@startuml state-transitions
title US-13: Alert State Machine

skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333

[*] --> NEW : alert persisted

NEW --> ACKNOWLEDGED : operator acknowledges
ACKNOWLEDGED --> RESOLVED : operator resolves
NEW --> RESOLVED : operator resolves directly

NEW --> SUPERSEDED : system correlation\nstronger COMPOSITE replaces individual alert
ACKNOWLEDGED --> SUPERSEDED : system correlation\nstronger COMPOSITE replaces individual alert

RESOLVED --> [*]
SUPERSEDED --> [*]

note right of NEW
  Initial durable state.
  Replayed delivery does not create another row
  because alert_id is deterministic.
end note

note right of ACKNOWLEDGED
  Operator handling state.
  A later composite may still supersede it;
  acknowledgement does not freeze correlation.
end note

note right of SUPERSEDED
  System-only terminal state.
  Used when a stronger COMPOSITE incident
  replaces an active individual alert.
  superseded_by points to the composite alert.
end note

note right of RESOLVED
  Operator terminal state.
  A recurrence creates a new alert_id;
  the old row is never reopened or overwritten.
end note

@enduml
